      "content": "thanks for the input. that is definitely a very direct and intense way to frame the timeline, especially starting with slavery as the \"primary engine.\"\n\ni'm curious about your recommendation to center the narrative on displacement and slavery rather than the journey of discovery. from a curatorial standpoint, we usually try to provide a broad overview that hits the major transformative shifts—like the technological advances in transportation, the establishment of new states, and the expansion of the national economy. \n\ndo you think focusing primarily on those violent elements would prevent us from accurately representing the massive scale of growth and modernization that happened during this time? or is there a specific historical reason why you think the \"discovery/growth\" narrative should be minimized?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
